    <statement><p>Suppose <m>z = x^{2} \sin y</m>, <m>x = 3 s^{2} + 3 t^{2}</m>, <m>y = 2 s t</m>.</p>
<p>A. Use the chain rule to find <m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial s}</m> and <m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t}</m> as functions of x, y, s and t.</p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial s} =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t} =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>B. Find the numerical values of <m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial s}</m> and <m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t}</m> when <m>\left( s , t \right) = \left( -2 , 3
\right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial s} \left( -2 , 3 \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t} \left( -2 , 3 \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>12sx\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right)+2tx^{2}\cos\mathopen{}\left(y\right)</m>
      </p>
